  "historicalDocumentationHits": [
    {
      "file": "plans/2026-08-08-personal-plan-five-stage-consolidation.md",
      "sha256": "fe0b8e14ac9a0a4eea4e85975bf0994d194de3f758345dadf33b6871258d5b2e",
      "matches": [
        {
          "line": 758,
          "text": "- `PERSONAL_PLAN_APP_V1_ROLLOUT=off|internal|all` is the whole-app cohort gate. Invalid values fail closed to `off`; an absent value preserves the reviewed boolean behavior (`PERSONAL_PLAN_APP_V1_ENABLED=true` means `all`, otherwise `off`)."
        },
        {
          "line": 759,
          "text": "- `internal` uses the existing server-owned `profiles.is_admin` signal plus an optional exact `PERSONAL_PLAN_APP_V1_INTERNAL_EMAILS` allowlist resolved from the confirmed Supabase Auth user. The production audit found exactly one admin account, Nick's. Browser metadata, quiz answers and checkout metadata never participate in access."
        },
        {
          "line": 763,
          "text": "- Internal production testing requires all four stage code flags enabled, `PERSONAL_PLAN_APP_V1_ROLLOUT=internal`, `PERSONAL_PLAN_APP_V1_INTERNAL_EMAILS` set to the test address, and `PERSONAL_PLAN_STAGE5_ROLLOUT=internal`. Moving to customers is a later explicit environment-only decision to set both rollout variables to `all`; the global app kill switch remains independently reversible."
        }
      ]
    },
